.DS_Store

# Real .eml samples for building the phase 4 paste/import pipeline against —
# real correspondence, kept out of this public repo's history on purpose.
# Fixtures derived from them (trimmed, reviewed) live in test/ instead.
/test-emails/

# Claude Code session scratch. The diagnostics skill under `.claude/skills/` is checked in
# — `CLAUDE.md` points at it — and these two are per-session state that is not.
.claude/RESUME.md
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# The UI kit: a PowerPoint parts bin and the ~70 PNGs it is built from, generated by
# `npm run ui:kit` and `npm run ui:deck`. Twelve megabytes of pictures that go stale the
# moment the renderer changes, and are rebuilt in minutes from the two scripts — which are
# checked in. `design/old/` holds earlier exports kept by hand.
#
# `design/` is ignored by default, so a new export folder stays out without anyone
# remembering to add it. Hand-written design work is named below to opt back in.
/design/*
!/design/design-handoff-pane-consistency/

# A rendered copy of a document whose source is checked in beside it. `ROADMAP.md` is the
# thing to read and to review a diff of; the PDF is one export of it, goes stale the moment
# the markdown is edited, and is a binary this repo's history has no use for. Same rule as
# `design/` above: the source is versioned, the artefact is not.
ROADMAP.pdf

# The venv `scripts/build-ui-deck.py` asks for. python-pptx is deliberately not a project
# dependency: it is needed to build a design asset, never to build or run the app.
/.venv/
